===Etymology 2===
{{etymid|en|art}}
From {{inh|en|enm|list}}, {{m|enm|liste||ability, cleverness, cunning, skill; adroitness, dexterity; strategem, trick; device, design, token}}, from {{inh|en|ang|list||art, craft; cleverness, cunning, experience, skill}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=list(e|pos=n.(1)|id=MED25748|accessdate=24 June 2018}}</ref> from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*listi}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*listiz||art, craft}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*leys-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*leyǝs-||furrow, trace, track, trail}}.

The word is cognate with {{cog|nl|list||artifice, guile, sleight; ruse, strategem}}, {{cog|de|List||cunning, guile; ploy, ruse, trick}}, {{cog|nds|list||artifice, cunning; prudence, wisdom}}, {{cog|is|list||art}}, {{cog|stq|list||cunning, knowledge}}, {{cog|sco|list||art, craft, skill; cunning}}, {{cog|sv|list||art; cunning, guile, wile; ruse, trick; stealth}}, and possibly {{cog|es|listo||clever}}. It is also related to {{m|en|learn}}, {{m|en|lore}}.

