===Etymology 4===
{{etymid|en|desire}}
From {{inh|en|enm|listen}}, {{m|enm|list}}, {{m|enm|liste}}, {{m|enm|leste}}, {{m|enm|lesten|t=to choose, desire, wish (to do something)}}, from {{inh|en|ang|lystan}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=listen|pos=v.(1)|id=MED25754|accessdate=17 June 2018}}</ref> from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*lustijan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*lustijaną}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*lustuz|t=pleasure}}.

The word is cognate with {{cog|stq|läste|t=to wish for, desire, crave}}, {{cog|fy|lêste|t=to like, desire}}, {{cog|nl|lusten|t=to appreciate, like; to lust}}, {{cog|de|lüsten}}, {{m|de|gelüsten|t=to desire, want, crave}}, {{cog|da|lyste|t=to desire, feel like, want}}, {{cog|fo|lysta|t=to desire}}.

